WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.022 --> 00:00:03.063
- [Narrator] This bright, colorful temple,

00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:04.861
located in southern India,

00:00:04.861 --> 00:00:07.459
wasn't put on earth just to catch the eye.

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:11.098
It's also one of the largest
Hindu houses of worship.

00:00:11.098 --> 00:00:14.535
Welcome to the Sri Ranganathaswamy Temple.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:17.618
(slow hip hop music)

00:00:21.305 --> 00:00:24.322
It is dedicated to the
Hindu god of Ranganatha,

00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:27.845
a reclining form of
the Hindu deity Vishnu.

00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:29.889
But this relaxed-looking god is one of the

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:32.389
highest levels of Hindu idols.

00:00:33.302 --> 00:00:35.899
The temple, which has
over six miles of walls

00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:37.683
and over 100 buildings,

00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:39.568
is one of the five
important pilgrimage sites

00:00:39.568 --> 00:00:44.556
along the river Kaveri,
for devotees of Ranganatha.

00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:46.644
The temple itself is a beacon of the

00:00:46.644 --> 00:00:50.835
uniquely South Indian Dravidian
style of architecture.

00:00:50.835 --> 00:00:53.526
Its temples are adorned
with pyramid-shaped towers

00:00:53.526 --> 00:00:57.173
made from sandstone,
soapstone, or granite.

00:00:57.173 --> 00:00:58.796
The first construction on this site

00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:01.302
dates back nearly 700 years.

00:01:01.302 --> 00:01:04.522
It grew and grew into the
wonder that it is today,

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:08.689
a site that will surely settle
any pilgrim's wandering soul.

00:01:13.286 --> 00:01:15.203
(bing)

